%description:
Tests TcpSocket::setPathMtu() with the path MTU search (mtuProbing = 2), in the
scenario of the Linux script mtu_probe/basic-v4. At the start, the route MTU is
that of the MSS of 600 (640). At t=0.9 s, the server application raises it to
1500, as the script does with ip route change. No probe goes above the route
MTU, so the search needs the larger MTU. Then the server sends the probe of 986
bytes (MTU 1026), as in tcp_mtu_probe_1, and its ACK raises the MSS to 986. The
larger route MTU does not raise the MSS by itself: the segments before the ACK
of the probe stay at 600.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

sim-time-limit = 5s
*.srv_app.sendScript="1.0 40000"
*.srv_app.pathMtuScript="0.9 1500"
*.srv_tcp.mss = 600
*.cli_tcp.mss = 1460
*.*_tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.srv_tcp.mtuProbing = 2
*.srv_tcp.baseMss = 512

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.017 B020] A.1000 < B.2000: A 11301:11901(600) ack 1 win 16384 
[1.017 B021] A.1000 < B.2000: A 11901:12887(986) ack 1 win 16384 
[1.017 B022] A.1000 < B.2000: A 12887:13487(600) ack 1 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
The route MTU is 1500, SMSS is 600
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: sent an MTU probe of 986 bytes (MTU 1026)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
RFC 4821: the MTU probe of 1026 is acknowledged, snd_mss is 986
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
